# SmartFlow Plugin Package Boundary

Use this Rule when writing or reviewing reusable SmartFlow plugin content.

The plugin package must be self-contained for consumers who only receive the `smartflow` plugin folder. A required workflow, safety, QA, documentation, or onboarding step must not depend on files elsewhere in this development repository.

## Required Checks

- Every required Skill, Rule, Agent, Command, reference, script, checklist, or workflow contract named by the plugin must exist inside the plugin package, which is `plugins/smartflow` in this development repository, or be explicitly marked as an optional external dependency.
- Default SmartFlow workflows must not require `.agents`, `.cursor/plugins/cache`, `weseo-smartflow-frontend-guide`, `Tests/`, `.scratch`, repository-local scripts, or any other development-only path.
- If a workflow says "run `<skill-name>`", that Skill must be bundled in `plugins/smartflow/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` unless the workflow clearly says the Skill is optional and external.
- If a workflow routes to a named subagent, that Agent definition must be bundled under `plugins/smartflow/agents/` unless the workflow clearly says the Agent is optional and external.
- `PROJECT-CONTEXT.md` and the project `docs/` layer are project-local artifacts created or updated in the opened project checkout. Do not reference a plugin-local copy unless this package actually bundles that file.
- Reusable guidance must not include real client IDs, server paths, URLs, credentials, token-bearing examples, repository names, WordPress roots, cache commands, editable path exceptions, ACF keys, field post IDs, WP Grid Builder IDs, or access values.
- Secret-handling guidance stays with project context: real access values must never be copied into reusable plugin content, tracked files, chat, diagnostics, screenshots, or public webroot artifacts.
- The plugin README, manifest, release notes, rules, skills, agents, and commands must agree on the bundled content list.
- Manifest `source` fields and archive references are development provenance only. Runtime `path` fields and required workflow references must point to bundled plugin content.

Stop and fix the package before shipping if a required workflow path points outside the plugin folder without being marked optional or project-local, or if reusable guidance contains project-only values.
